# Binaries
#
# `go build ./...` drops a binary named after each main package in the working
# directory. examples/receipt is the one that exists today.
#
# Named by its full path, because the two shorter forms are both wrong. A
# leading `/receipt` anchors to the repository root and matched nothing — which
# is how a 9MB binary reached git six times. A bare `receipt` matches at any
# depth and therefore matches the *directory* examples/receipt/, quietly making
# every new file in it invisible to `git add`.
examples/receipt/receipt
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/bin/
/dist/

# Where the Makefile puts binaries it builds on purpose, so that nothing lands
# beside its source (see the note above).
/.bin/

# Test and coverage output
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
/eval/report/*.local.*

# Fuzzing corpus additions found by the fuzzer
testdata/fuzz/

# Go workspace — local to each contributor
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Environment
.env
.env.*
